#version 450
// ports/vulkan/shaders/ring_inc.comp - THE DOORBELL RING, AS A RECORDED DEVICE OPERATION.
// ============================================================================================================
// The engine's own requirement, quoted from `src/core/layer.cpp:383-389`:
//
//   "THE RING LIVES IN A .cu ... The sequence value is read from the HOST copy and incremented, which is what
//    makes the write idempotent across replays of the same graph - a captured literal would ring the same
//    number forever and the host would never see a change."
//
// `src/kernels/cuda/elementwise.cu:209-212` (`doorbell_ring_kernel`) is a one-thread kernel that does exactly
// this.  Its Vulkan form is this shader: the ring lives in a HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_COHERENT region (the shim's
// `cudaHostAlloc` maps a device block, so the host's `h_seq` and the device's buffer are ONE allocation), and
// the increment RE-READS it, so a captured-then-replayed block advances the ring on every replay instead of
// replaying a stale literal.
//
// WHY THE DISPATCH IS WHAT MAKES IT RIGHT: the host path (`Ctx::dispatch`) RECORDS while a stream capture is
// active and submits-and-waits otherwise (`vk_compute.cpp`).  So one definition of the ring serves both the
// direct case (a fenced submit: the host sees the new value on return) and the captured-block case (a recorded
// node: re-executed - and re-read - by every replay).
//
// ONE PUSH CONSTANT SELECTS THE TWO ENGINE VARIANTS:
//   store == 0  -> the read-modify-write INCREMENT (`doorbell_publish` / `doorbell_ring` / `_res`), the
//                  forward-path ring.
//   store != 0  -> STORE `value` (`doorbell_publish_value`, the HIP STRATA_DOORBELL_STORE=1 / P6-verifier
//                  variant whose CUDA form stores a kernel argument - a capture-time constant by design, and
//                  NOT on the forward path).
// A single lane writes; the workgroup size matches the host's `kLocalSize` (every dispatch this backend issues
// is sized from it, and the gate checks the agreement).
layout(local_size_x = 256) in;
layout(push_constant) uniform PC { uint value; uint store; } pc;
layout(set = 0, binding = 0, std430) buffer Seq { uint seq; } ring;
void main() {
    if (gl_GlobalInvocationID.x == 0u)
        ring.seq = (pc.store != 0u) ? pc.value : (ring.seq + 1u);
}
